--- Overview
Shows the orchestrator's hostname in the web UI, because the UI is usually reached over a forwarded port that doesn't identify the host. Fatal startup errors written to stderr now also carry a timestamp.

--- Key Changes
  * orchestrator (main.go)
    * Fatal errors written to stderr now start with an RFC3339 timestamp, since they can happen before slog is set up.
  * webui (API)
    * Added an optional hostname field to the BuildInfo schema in openapi.yaml; it is left out when the OS reports no name.
    * CurrentBuildInfo fills in Hostname from os.Hostname(); an error or empty name leaves it unset.
    * Tests check the hostname in TestCurrentBuildInfo and the /buildinfo endpoint.
  * webui (frontend)
    * The header shows the hostname next to the title, and the browser tab title becomes <host> * Runner Orchestrator.
    * ConfigView has a new "Host" row.
    * Added styling for the host label and rebuilt the dist assets.

--- Breaking Changes
None
